# XL project context

Before substantive edits to this repository, read **`AGENTS.md`** at the repo
root. It documents comment style, type inference pitfalls (`Types::Evaluate`,
`rcalls`, `evalInProgress`), and debugging with recorder traces.

When the user gives important style or convention guidance—or corrects an
assistant mistake—**update `AGENTS.md`** in that turn (see “How to maintain”
there). Keep boxed function comments to one “what” line inside the box; put
“why” and implementation detail below the closing rule line, with lines ≤ 80
characters.

Detailed enforcement for `src/**/*.cpp` and `src/**/*.h`: see
**`.cursor/rules/xl-cpp-boxed-comments.mdc`**.
